/T (recursion? The process in which a function calls itself directly or indirectly is called recursion and the corresponding function is called a  recursive function. Recursive algorithm is essential to divide and conquer paradigm, whereby the idea is to divide bigger problems  into smaller subproblems and the subproblem is some constant fraction of the original problem. The way recursion works is by  solving the smaller subproblems individually and then aggregating the results to return the final solution.)
/E (recursion? The process in which a function calls itself directly or indirectly is called recursion and the corresponding function is called a  recursive function. Recursive algorithm is essential to divide and conquer paradigm, whereby the idea is to divide bigger problems  into smaller subproblems and the subproblem is some constant fraction of the original problem. The way recursion works is by  solving the smaller subproblems individually and then aggregating the results to return the final solution.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [14]
>>
