3225 0 obj
<<
/Title (Linear probing If a pair is hashed to a slot which is already occupied, it searches linearly for the next free slot in the table. Chaining The hash table will be an array of linked lists. All keys mapping to the same index will be stored as linked list nodes at that index. Resizing the hash table The size of the hash table can be increased in order to spread the hash entries further apart. A threshold value signifies the  percentage of the hash-table that needs to be occupied before resizing. A hash table with a threshold of 0.6 would resize when 60%  of the space is occupied. As a convention, the size of the hash-table is doubled. This can be memory intensive.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3222 0 R
>>
endobj
