3228 0 obj
<<
/Title (Hash tables have incredibly quick lookups, but remember that we need a reliable collision solution; normally, we don't need to worry about this because our language in the computer beneath the hood takes care of it for us. It allows us to respond quickly, and depending on the type of hash table, such as maps in JavaScript, we can have flexible keys instead of an array with 0 1 2 3 only numbered indexes. The disadvantage of hash tables is that they are unordered. It's difficult to go through everything in an orderly fashion. Furthermore, it has slow key iteration. That is, if I want to retrieve all the keys from a hash table, I have to navigate the  entire memory space.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3226 0 R
>>
endobj
